   "text": "This SMILES is a transcription of the drawing, and I could not run a validity check on it. I read the molecule as a cyclic peptide with a disulfide bridge, written from the C-terminal glycinamide toward the N-terminus.\n\n**Main chain, C-terminus to N-terminus**\n- Glycinamide carrying an N-methyl group, then 3-pyridylalanine, Asn and Glu.\n- The Glu nitrogen is joined through a urea (NH\u2013C(=O)\u2013NH) to the carbonyl of a 4-aminotetrahydropyran-4-carboxylic acid unit.\n- Next come 2-naphthylalanine and Tyr whose phenol oxygen carries \u2013CH2CH2NH2.\n- The macrocycle runs Pen, Lys(Ac), 7-methyl-Trp, Thr, Lys, Pen, with the two Pen sulfurs bonded as S\u2013S. I wrote the disulfide with ring-closure label %10.\n- The last residue is Arg, acylated at its N-terminus by C(=O)CH2CH2OCH2CH2OCH2CH2N\u207a(CH3)3.\n\n**Lys side chain on the right**\n- Lys \u03b5-N\u2013C(=O)CH2OCH2CH2OCH2CH2NH\u2013C(=O)CH2OCH2CH2OCH2CH2NH\u2013C(=O)CH2CH2\u2013\u03b3-Glu.\n- The \u03b3-Glu \u03b1-nitrogen is acylated by an 18-carbon diacid chain (C(=O), 16 CH2, COOH). I counted 18 carbons from the drawn chain length, so the CH2 count is an estimate.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\n- From the wedges and hashes, every \u03b1-carbon works out as the L-configuration: Pal, Asn, Glu, Nal, Tyr, Lys, Trp, Arg and \u03b3-Glu are S, and both Pen are R, which is L-Pen.\n- Thr is (2S,3R).\n- I wrote each residue as `C(=O)[C@H](R)N`, and the Thr \u03b2-carbon as `[C@@H](C)O`, to encode these.\n\nSMILES: NC(=O)CN(C)C(=O)[C@H](Cc1cccnc1)NC(=O)[C@H](CC(N)=O)NC(=O)[C@H](CCC(=O)O)NC(=O)NC(=O)C1(CCOCC1)NC(=O)[C@H](Cc1ccc2ccccc2c1)NC(=O)[C@H](Cc1ccc(OCCN)cc1)NC(=O)[C@H](C(C)(C)S%10)NC(=O)[C@H](CCCCNC(C)=O)NC(=O)[C@H](Cc1c[nH]c2c(C)cccc12)NC(=O)[C@H]([C@@H](C)O)NC(=O)[C@H](CCCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)CC[C@H](NC(=O)CCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCC(=O)O)C(=O)O)NC(=O)[C@H](C(C)(C)S%10)NC(=O)[C@H](CCCNC(=N)N)NC(=O)CCOCCOCC[N+](C)(C)C"
